Uncontainable
-------------

Some might say
it's a cliché:
that I'm just saying
what I'm 'sposed to say.
They might say I'm
unoriginal.
Well, I don't care
at all,
because You know
I'm being real.
I'm just saying
how I feel.

This love You placed in me
is uncontainable
(my heart bursts at the seams).
Your goodness and great deeds
are incomparable
(I praise the God who redeems).

Trying to say
how my spirit soars
when I think of the goodness
of my Lord;
trying to express
my gratitude
knowing each good gift
comes from You.
Searching for a way
to exclaim
the beauty, the wonder
of Your name.

This love You placed in me
is uncontainable
(my heart bursts at the seams).
Your goodness and great deeds
are incomparable
(I praise the God who redeems).

For He who is mighty
has done great things for me,
and holy is His Name.
For those who fear Him,
He has abounding mercy,
from generation to generation.

So here I offer
my humble verse,
to say how my heart
begins to burst
when thoughts of You
fill my mind
and I ponder
Your love divine,
when I remember
Your great might,
and am assured
You hold me tight.

This love You placed in me
is uncontainable
(my heart bursts at the seams).
Your goodness and great deeds
are incomparable
(I praise the God who redeems).
